MATCH (a:Package) WHERE a.name IN ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd', 'e', 'f', 'g', 'h', 'i', 'j', 'k', 'l', 'm', 'n', 'o', 'p', 'q'] RETURN a
  -> at 1:32 cypher: not supported yet: a WHERE of more than 16 alternatives (jaala#388): this WHERE expands to more than 16 alternatives

## refused plainly

MATCH (a:Package) RETURN a.name SKIP 1
  -> at 1:19 cypher: SKIP needs an ORDER BY here, so a page continues from a stable order

MATCH (a:Package) RETURN a.name ORDER BY a.license
  -> at 1:42 cypher: ORDER BY has to name a column RETURN writes (add it to RETURN, or order by its alias)

SHOW INDEXES
  -> at 1:1 cypher: SHOW is a command for the database, not a query: only a query compiles

SHOW DATABASES YIELD name
  -> at 1:1 cypher: SHOW is a command for the database, not a query: only a query compiles

CREATE INDEX package_name FOR (a:Package) ON (a.name)
  -> at 1:1 cypher: CREATE is a command for the database, not a query: only a query compiles

CREATE CONSTRAINT FOR (a:Package) REQUIRE a.name IS UNIQUE
  -> at 1:1 cypher: CREATE is a command for the database, not a query: only a query compiles

DROP INDEX package_name
  -> at 1:1 cypher: DROP is a command for the database, not a query: only a query compiles

GRANT TRAVERSE ON GRAPH * TO reader
  -> at 1:1 cypher: GRANT is a command for the database, not a query: only a query compiles

EXPLAIN MATCH (a:Package) RETURN a
  -> at 1:1 cypher: EXPLAIN plans the query without answering it: leave EXPLAIN out

MATCH (a:Package) FINISH
  -> at 1:19 cypher: FINISH answers nothing: end the query with RETURN

MATCH (a:Package) WHERE a.license = null RETURN a
  -> at 1:37 cypher: null never equals anything: write IS NULL or IS NOT NULL

MATCH (a:Package) RETURN true
  -> at 1:26 cypher: jaala has no booleans: compare a property with the value the graph stores

MATCH (a:Package) RETURN a LIMIT 0
  -> at 1:34 cypher: LIMIT 0 answers nothing: leave the query out

